    <item>
      <title>Mushtaq: Doctor to Coding Architect (Expertease Podcast #5)</title>
      <link>/2021/10/31/31-podcast-expertease-mushtaq-doctor-to-architect/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 31 Oct 2021 02:13:50 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>/2021/10/31/31-podcast-expertease-mushtaq-doctor-to-architect/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Listen On: &lt;a href=&#34;https://open.spotify.com/show/1jA35fmXfHzNoiauVLoU8B&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Spotify&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://anchor.fm/expertease&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Anchor.fm&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://podcasts.apple.com/in/podcast/expertease/id1524690855&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Apple&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://podcasts.google.com/feed/aHR0cHM6Ly9hbmNob3IuZm0vcy8yY2JhOGVmOC9wb2RjYXN0L3Jzcw==&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Google Podcasts&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;iframe &#xA;        src=&#34;//anchor.fm/expertease/embed/episodes/Episode-5---From-Doctor-to-Coding-Architect-with-Mushtaq-Ahmed-Expertease-e19ihf1&#34;&#xA;        height=&#34;204px&#34; &#xA;        width=&#34;775px&#34; &#xA;        frameborder=&#34;0&#34; &#xA;        scrolling=&#34;no&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;mushtaq-ahmed-from-doctor-to-coding-architect---episode-5&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Mushtaq Ahmed: From Doctor to Coding Architect - Episode #5&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#mushtaq-ahmed-from-doctor-to-coding-architect---episode-5&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this episode on &lt;a href=&#34;https://anchor.fm/expertease&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;&lt;em&gt;Expertease&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, we have an honest and insightful conversation with a dear friend and colleague &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/in/mushtaq-ahmed-a0b76b/?originalSubdomain=in&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Mushtaq Ahmed&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, Principal Consultant at Thoughtworks Pune.&#xA;We cover topics ranging from his interests, his journey from studying to be a Doctor, then becoming a BA, then a Developer and now a Senior Technical Leader;&#xA;and his passion for programming. He is a Scala evangelist. In the later part of the podcast we discuss his work with Thirty Meter Telescope and architecture principles for building systems at Astronomical scale.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Insights on Career, Mastery and Craftsmanship (Expertease Podcast #4)</title>
      <link>/2020/11/29/podcast-building-engineering-career-nikhil-prasad/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 29 Nov 2020 02:13:50 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>/2020/11/29/podcast-building-engineering-career-nikhil-prasad/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Listen On: &lt;a href=&#34;https://open.spotify.com/show/1jA35fmXfHzNoiauVLoU8B&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Spotify&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://anchor.fm/expertease&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Anchor.fm&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://podcasts.apple.com/in/podcast/expertease/id1524690855&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Apple&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://podcasts.google.com/feed/aHR0cHM6Ly9hbmNob3IuZm0vcy8yY2JhOGVmOC9wb2RjYXN0L3Jzcw==&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Google Podcasts&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;iframe &#xA;        src=&#34;//anchor.fm/expertease/embed/episodes/Episode-4---Insights-on-Career--Mastery-and-Craftsmanship-with-Nikhil-Prasad-Expertease-en49op&#34;&#xA;        height=&#34;204px&#34; &#xA;        width=&#34;775px&#34; &#xA;        frameborder=&#34;0&#34; &#xA;        scrolling=&#34;no&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;nikhil-prasad-part1---empowered-engineering-culture---episode-3&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Nikhil Prasad (Part1) - Empowered Engineering Culture - Episode #3&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#nikhil-prasad-part1---empowered-engineering-culture---episode-3&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In Part 1 of our conversation with &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/in/nikhilprasad/?originalSubdomain=in&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Nikhil Prasad&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, CTO and co-founder of &lt;a href=&#34;https://tavisca.com&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;tavisca&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, we discussed ways &amp;amp; means of building an empowered Engineering culture, and how Mastery, Autonomy and Purpose play a key role in building a vibrant company culture. You can listen to the insighful conversation here: &lt;a href=&#34;/2020/10/02/podcast-empowered-engineers-nikhil-prasad.html&#34; &gt;Nikhil Prasad - Part 1 - Engineering culture&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Empowered Engineering Culture - Nikhil Prasad (Expertease Podcast #3)</title>
      <link>/2020/10/02/podcast-empowered-engineers-nikhil-prasad/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2020 02:13:50 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>/2020/10/02/podcast-empowered-engineers-nikhil-prasad/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Listen On: &lt;a href=&#34;https://open.spotify.com/show/1jA35fmXfHzNoiauVLoU8B&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Spotify&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://anchor.fm/expertease&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Anchor.fm&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://podcasts.apple.com/in/podcast/expertease/id1524690855&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Apple&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://podcasts.google.com/feed/aHR0cHM6Ly9hbmNob3IuZm0vcy8yY2JhOGVmOC9wb2RjYXN0L3Jzcw==&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Google Podcasts&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;iframe &#xA;        src=&#34;//anchor.fm/expertease/embed/episodes/Episode-3---Empowered-Engineering-Culture-with-Nikhil-Prasad-Expertease-ekg2mi/a-a3dt5e3&#34;&#xA;        height=&#34;204px&#34; &#xA;        width=&#34;775px&#34; &#xA;        frameborder=&#34;0&#34; &#xA;        scrolling=&#34;no&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;nikhil-prasad---cultivating-an-empowered-engineering-culture-part1&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Nikhil Prasad - Cultivating an Empowered Engineering Culture (Part1)&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#nikhil-prasad---cultivating-an-empowered-engineering-culture-part1&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this third episode of &lt;a href=&#34;https://anchor.fm/expertease&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;&lt;em&gt;Expertease&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, we have an insightful chat with &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/in/nikhilprasad/?originalSubdomain=in&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Nikhil Prasad&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, CTO and co-founder of &lt;a href=&#34;https://tavisca.com&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;tavisca&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, a 700 people, product company, that is considered to be a strong people-centric organisation in Pune.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img src=&#34;/images/general/podcast3/nikhilprasad.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Nikhil Prasad&#34; &gt;&#xA;    &lt;figcaption &#xA;    &#x9;style=&#34; &#xA;    &#x9;font-style: italic; &#xA;    &#x9;text-align: center; &#xA;    &#x9;color: grey; &#xA;    &#x9;font-size: 14px&#34;&#xA;    &#x9;&gt;&#xA;    &#x9;Nikhil Prasad&#xA;    &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Exiting the Rat Race -  The Entrepreneurial Journey of Sandeep Nanu (Expertease Podcast #2)</title>
      <link>/2020/08/01/podcast-exiting-the-rat-race-sandeep-nanu/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2020 02:13:50 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>/2020/08/01/podcast-exiting-the-rat-race-sandeep-nanu/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Listen On: &lt;a href=&#34;https://open.spotify.com/episode/1FoVRmsLITegc3iCiGL7ex&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Spotify&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://anchor.fm/expertease&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Anchor.fm&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://podcasts.apple.com/in/podcast/expertease/id1524690855&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Apple&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://podcasts.google.com/feed/aHR0cHM6Ly9hbmNob3IuZm0vcy8yY2JhOGVmOC9wb2RjYXN0L3Jzcw==&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Google Podcasts&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;iframe &#xA;        src=&#34;//anchor.fm/expertease/embed/episodes/Episode-2---Exiting-the-Rat-Race---The-Entrepreneurial-Journey-of-Sandeep-Nanu-ehha23/a-a2rcgob&#34;&#xA;        height=&#34;204px&#34; &#xA;        width=&#34;775px&#34; &#xA;        frameborder=&#34;0&#34; &#xA;        scrolling=&#34;no&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;sandeep-nanu---exiting-the-rat-race&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Sandeep Nanu - Exiting the Rat Race&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#sandeep-nanu---exiting-the-rat-race&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this second episode of &lt;a href=&#34;https://anchor.fm/expertease&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;&lt;em&gt;Expertease&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, we have a spirited chat with &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/in/sandeepnanu/?originalSubdomain=in&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Sandeep Nanu&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, serial entrepreneur and founder of a brand and communication consulting firm &lt;a href=&#34;https://writeclick.in/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;WriteClick&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img src=&#34;/images/general/podcast2/Sandeep_Nanu1.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;Sandeep Nanu&#34; &gt;&#xA;    &lt;figcaption &#xA;    &#x9;style=&#34; &#xA;    &#x9;font-style: italic; &#xA;    &#x9;text-align: center; &#xA;    &#x9;color: grey; &#xA;    &#x9;font-size: 14px&#34;&#xA;    &#x9;&gt;&#xA;    &#x9;Sandeep Nanu&#xA;    &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Sandeep talks about his first job as a WebDesigner and the lessons he learnt there, including the important of respecting your commitments to other and their time. We discuss his first company, CBeyond &amp;ndash; his challenges in dealing with large corporations and his motivation to instead find a better way to work sustainably, which led him to start WriteClick eventually in 2010.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Art of Experience Design with Aditya Karle (Expertease Podcast #1)</title>
      <link>/2020/07/22/podcast-art-of-experience-design/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2020 02:13:50 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>/2020/07/22/podcast-art-of-experience-design/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Listen On: &lt;a href=&#34;https://open.spotify.com/episode/2QTq4UjyQoWx5jOZbgRQXr&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Spotify&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://anchor.fm/expertease&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Anchor.fm&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://podcasts.apple.com/in/podcast/expertease/id1524690855&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Apple&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://podcasts.google.com/feed/aHR0cHM6Ly9hbmNob3IuZm0vcy8yY2JhOGVmOC9wb2RjYXN0L3Jzcw==&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Google Podcasts&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;iframe &#xA;        src=&#34;//anchor.fm/expertease/embed/episodes/Episode-1---Art-of-Experience-Design-with-Aditya-Karle-Expertease-eh360u/a-a2ormjc&#34;&#xA;        height=&#34;204px&#34; &#xA;        width=&#34;775px&#34; &#xA;        frameborder=&#34;0&#34; &#xA;        scrolling=&#34;no&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;description&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Description&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#description&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this first episode of &lt;a href=&#34;https://anchor.fm/expertease&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;&lt;em&gt;Expertease&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, we have a light-hearted chat with &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/in/adityakarle/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; &gt;Aditya Karle&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;, Head of Design at ThoughtWorks India, to deconstruct the art of Experience Design (XD).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img src=&#34;/images/general/podcast1/aditya-karle.jpeg&#34; alt=&#34;Aditya Karle&#34; &gt;&#xA;    &lt;figcaption &#xA;    &#x9;style=&#34; &#xA;    &#x9;font-style: italic; &#xA;    &#x9;text-align: center; &#xA;    &#x9;color: grey; &#xA;    &#x9;font-size: 14px&#34;&#xA;    &#x9;&gt;&#xA;    &#x9;Aditya Karle&#xA;    &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1:10:&lt;/strong&gt; We talk about his journey to becoming a Designer and getting involved in Software Design, discuss differences between UI design, UX and XD.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Understanding Open Source Software</title>
      <link>/2017/03/12/open-source-explained/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 12 Mar 2017 02:13:50 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>/2017/03/12/open-source-explained/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&#xA;  &lt;figure&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img src=&#34;/images/general/guitar.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;My acoustic guitar - Greg Bennett&#34; &gt;&#xA;    &lt;figcaption &#xA;    &#x9;style=&#34; &#xA;    &#x9;font-style: italic; &#xA;    &#x9;text-align: center; &#xA;    &#x9;color: grey; &#xA;    &#x9;font-size: 14px&#34;&#xA;    &#x9;&gt;&#xA;    &#x9;My acoustic guitar - Greg Bennett&#xA;    &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have been contributing to Open Source Software (OSS) for over 3 years now, at ThoughtWorks. Many people seem to have some misconceptions about OSS, or don’t fully realise the implications and impact of OSS. In this blog, I have shared a few  of my learnings and thoughts on this topic. If you are technologist – who has some familiarity with OSS, then it’s likely that this article will be helpful.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
